to some of the newly uploaded shorts
pointing to July 30th.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.460
This is the day where

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.000
all the original creators will be killed
and the clone invasion will be complete.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.780
So, is that it?

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:54.900
Is all hope lost for these shorts creators
as these half rate clones

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.120
come in and just take over the content?
Thankfully, no.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:59.520
The O.G. creators are fighting back
from the inside.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.520
All through the videos, they leave notes
saying that they're still alive.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:05.940
With Jonny RaZeR somehow
surviving being shot seven times.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:09.060
Now he himself is hatching a plan
behind the scenes to get into the facility

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:13.140
and save the day using a special flash
drive that he somehow magically obtained.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.120
How? Don't ask, at least not yet.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.800
But the clock is ticking.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.960
They don't have much time before
July 30th comes to pass,

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.700
and many of the creators are killed
for good.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.140
Namely, both RoyalPear

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:25.440
and Riggy are in the most immediate danger
as both are currently being held

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.700
in the clone VPN facility.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.020
But they're not going to take it lying
down.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.040
On July 29th,

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:32.280
Danno uploaded a short where clone Riggy
finally goes off the deep end.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.080
A QR code is hidden
at the end of this one,

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.280
leading us to a then-unlisted video titled
WhereDidRiggyGo.mp4.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.460
Here we see both Riggy and Pear
being interrogated by their clones.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:45.120
But Riggy is able to escape,
free Pear and book it towards an exit.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:48.300
Interestingly, the end card of this one
actually takes us to another video

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:51.300
with audio of a conversation
between clone Riggy and the Boss.

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:52.080
And let's just say that

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.020
the boss man is not happy
with RoyalPear and Riggy's escape.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.400
And we learn that the two found

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.860
the facility's control room
while exiting the building.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:09.900
Realizing that they're PNG Tubers
and therefore two dimensional, Riggy

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.140
and Pear slip through the door
and they see that the Boss’s plan is way

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.597
bigger than they ever realized.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:26.220
Yep. The boss's big plan
is to use his VPN sponsorship to clone

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.700
every short's tuber and replace them
with just garbage content.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.190
And given how widespread VPN sponsorships
are, I’m

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.020
guessing he's going to be able
to get every single YouTuber

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:35.460
on the platform in less than a month.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.340
But thankfully, there's a way
to stop his plan once and for all.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.760
If they pull all the codes together and
use the energy to overload the machine,

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:45.660
they can use that power to create a virus
that'll knock out Clone VPN forever.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:46.860
What then, is the code?

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.480
Well, here's where things get really cool.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.860
Remember when all the clones did

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.660
those sponsorship videos back
when they first took over?

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:54.000
Well, each video ends with a promo code
that features

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.940
2 to 3 characters, their name,
and then a number 1 to 5.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.460
Now, I saw this and knew
it had to mean something.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.620
By removing the creator names
and then ordering

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:04.140
what's left by those numbers at the end.
You get this.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.900
Now surprisingly,
that isn't a YouTube video ID,

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.760
even though it's
the same length and format.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:09.480
So I assumed that

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.880
it was some sort of a code or a cipher,
but that also didn't work.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:13.680
We just didn't
have all the information at the time.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.780
This is what that code is for.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:18.360
It was yet another masterful troll.
And I've got to admit, this time.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.400
This time they definitely got me.
But there's a problem.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.680
They need someone on the outside
to enter the code.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:25.980
Thankfully, they remember that
Joe Caine refused the deal and hasn't

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:26.580
been captured.

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:40.020
Scanning the QR code that pops up on
screen sends us to another secret video

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.540
where Joe puts the code into the Clone
VPN website,

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:46.020
which lets Riggy and Pear create
the virus, a virus that just so happens

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:49.200
to teleport
into the possession of Jonny RaZeR. Yup.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.580
That's where he got the drive from.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.800
A fact
that the boss realizes in real time.

00:15:12.114 --> 00:15:14.520
Though we don't actually see it happen,
RaZeR uploads

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:17.580
the virus, which then allows
each of the creators to have a 1v1 battle

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:21.420
against their clones to regain control
and end this saga once and for all.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.180
With the creators victorious, we’re
treated to a post-credits

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.400
scene where the Boss and clone
Riggy vow to come back.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.340
And then it's here
that we get our big twist ending.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.320
The flannel.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.140
Jonny RaZeR was The Boss the entire time.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:53.880
No, that's not possible.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.880
But, but no, really,
that's literally not possible. Right?

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:58.800
If Jonny was the one
who uploaded the virus

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.360
and saved the day,
that means that he played

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.460
an integral part in his own plan failing?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.780
Doesn't really make a whole lot of sense.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.040
I mean, sure, maybe you could argue

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.860
that Riggy did the smart thing
and went to the server room by himself.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:11.100
But this post ARG Q&amp;A
stream seems to argue otherwise.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.540
Even if we ignore these non-canon
live streams.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.060
In the logic of the show,
Jonny can't be the big boss.

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.800
Remember earlier, when The Boss said this?

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.340
It doesn't make sense
why he'd both pretend to hate RaZeR

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.800
and then openly admit that he's RaZeR
in the very next scene.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.320
So no,
this man can't be the real Jonny RaZeR.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.640
So is it a clone then?

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:45.840
Jonny's clone is.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.540
Yeah, he's not having the best time.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:55.140
So if The Boss is neither
the real or clone version of Jonny RaZeR,

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.000
then who is he? A third clone? PewDiePie?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:00.060
Me? This is where I have to wave
the white flag, at least for now.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:01.440
I don't think there's quite
enough information

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:03.000
out there to solve that mystery

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.000
just yet, and I suspect
that The Boss's identity will be revealed

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.840
when Shorts War has its season two,
which I, for one, am totally stoked for.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.500
I got to say,

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.680
this is got to be one of the coolest ARGs
that I've seen happen across YouTube.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.720
And what's more,
I believe the story that these

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.440
creators told has a lot more meaning
than just a bunch of clones taking over.

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:22.500
See, while watching this, I kept coming
back to the question, What's the point?

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.320
And I don't mean that in a harsh, like,
‘why do they make this?’ sort of way.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.620
No, I wanted to know what theme they were
trying to communicate through all this.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:32.760
And I believe that we find that in
the entire concept of this thing, Clones.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.680
The story of this
first season of the Shorts

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.320
War is a commentary
on cloned content across the Internet.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.180
I'm sure you've seen these sorts of things
around before.

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.340
Either
YouTube channels or Tiktoks or whatever

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:44.880
will just rip content from other websites
and re-upload them trying to make a quick

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.260
buck off of someone else's work.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:49.260
It's a problem that we here at theorist
have to deal with all the time,

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.260
and it's something that Jonny
RaZeR himself even talked about before

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.940
the Shorts War ARG began.

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.240
This, I believe, is
what sparked the whole idea of ARG.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.040
See, the clones that we see in the series

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.700
could never truly replace the creators
because they aren't those creators.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.100
Riggy actually
sums it up perfectly in one of his shorts.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:20.700
Those real world clone Tik Tok accounts
might be able to steal and upload videos,

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.740
but they're never going to be
those creators.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.440
A person's work is a culmination
of their own experiences

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.360
and insights, their successes
and their failures

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.820
all wrapped up into a person
with their own thoughts and feelings.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.580
And in the story,
I think that the clones realize this,

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:35.400
or at least some of them do,
like RoyalPear’s clone.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.620
During one of his shorts,
he seems to have second thoughts

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:40.140
about all the mindless creation of content
that's now his life.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:57.660
And later, as he's interrogating the real
RoyalPear, the clone feels bad about it.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.140
He's only doing it

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.920
because his boss, the algorithm
that needs content, is demanding it.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:07.200
But here's the thing,
there's another path in all of this.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.320
You can take the content of a creator
that you love and do your own pass.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.840
You can use it as inspiration
to create your own art.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:16.140
Even if it's similar to the people
who inspired you, it'll be uniquely yours

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.460
because you're the one who made it.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:20.460
And here's the spoiler alert
Nothing is ever wholly original anymore.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:23.340
I mean, Mozart and Da Vinci didn't
create their own works in a vacuum.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.740
They were inspired by what they enjoyed
looking at and listening to.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.960
Your favorite YouTubers, exactly the same.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:31.020
Here's Jonny RaZeR's thoughts
before they started the ARG.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.080
Couldn't have said it better myself
Jonny.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.960
I was pretty darn inspired
by all of your collective work.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.960
Onward to season two, my friends. But hey!

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:04.560
That's just a theory. A FILM THEORY!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.240
aaaaaaaand cut.

